{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.193,
   "text": "The drive-thru headset at my job has one rule taped inside it."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.793,
   "end": 13.273,
   "text": "If someone orders and the lane is empty... don't read the order back."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.173,
   "end": 21.064,
   "text": "The guy who worked nights before me wrote it. Marcus. He walked out in the middle of a shift and never came back."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.864,
   "end": 26.685,
   "text": "Three a.m. Rain on the menu board. Then the car sensor chimed."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.085,
   "end": 31.627,
   "text": "A soft voice in my ear. Just one, please."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.827,
   "end": 37.904,
   "text": "I checked the camera. The lane was empty. Just rain, shining under the lights."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.504,
   "end": 40.253,
   "text": "I didn't say a word."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 41.653,
   "end": 48.949,
   "text": "The voice waited. Then the sensor chimed again. And again. Like something was rolling closer... one slow inch at a time."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.949,
   "end": 55.261,
   "text": "Then the order printer clicked on by itself. One ticket. One line. My name."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 56.461,
   "end": 59.469,
   "text": "Read it back to me, the voice whispered."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 61.269,
   "end": 66.24,
   "text": "I ripped the headset off. And on the camera... the lane wasn't empty anymore."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 67.24,
   "end": 72.659,
   "text": "A long line of cars stretched out into the dark. Headlights off. Engines silent."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 73.659,
   "end": 77.989,
   "text": "The first one rolled up to my window. Marcus was driving."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 79.389,
   "end": 84.659,
   "text": "He smiled, held up a ticket with my name on it... and said, Order's ready."
  }
 ],
